open-source projects and respects their licenses:

  * Ultralytics YOLO (YOLO26) — AGPL-3.0 / Enterprise License.
    https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
    NOTE: The Ultralytics package is AGPL-3.0. If you redistribute a service
    that uses Ultralytics weights/code, you must comply with AGPL-3.0 or hold
    an Ultralytics Enterprise License. RailVision AI treats YOLO26 as a
    pluggable, swappable detector behind the `BaseDetector` interface so the
    core platform remains MIT-licensed.
  * OpenCV — Apache-2.0
  * PyTorch — BSD-3-Clause
  * FastAPI — MIT
